<title>SOUTH AFRICA: JCI may sell stake in Con Mrch.</title>
<headline>JCI may sell stake in Con Mrch.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mining house JCI Ltd said on Thursday that negotiations were underway which could lead to it selling its interests in antimony producer Consolidated Murchison Ltd.  </p>
<p>JCI is the principal shareholder in the company which mines in the Letaba district of South Africa for antimony ore, from which it produces antimony concentrates. Gold and silver are recovered as by-products.</p>
<p>Shareholders were urged to exercise caution in their dealings pending a further announcement.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
